# Cross-Sectional Asset Pricing Framework — Walkthrough

Implementation of the Uddin, Akter, and Hassan (2026) framework for predicting monthly excess returns of S&P 500 stocks using 510 covariates, 39 technical indicators, and 6 machine learning models.

---

## Project Structure

```
BTP/
├── config.py                      # Central configuration
├── requirements.txt               # Python dependencies
├── main.py                        # Pipeline orchestrator
├── data/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   └── download.py                # 6 data source downloaders
├── features/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── firm_chars.py              # 124 C&Z characteristics
│   ├── macro.py                   # PCA + 496 interactions
│   ├── technical.py               # 39 technical indicators
│   └── builder.py                 # 510-covariate matrix assembly
├── preprocessing/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   └── pipeline.py                # Exclusion + ffill + mean imputation
├── models/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── linear.py                  # OLS + LASSO
│   ├── tree.py                    # Decision Tree + Random Forest
│   ├── boosting.py                # XGBoost/GBRT
│   └── deep_nn.py                 # PyTorch Deep-NN (5 layers)
├── training/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   └── rolling_window.py          # Expanding window evaluator
└── analysis/
    ├── __init__.py
    ├── shap_analysis.py           # SHAP on Deep-NN
    ├── portfolio_sorts.py         # Quintile sorts + H-L
    ├── dm_test.py                 # Diebold-Mariano test
    └── uncertainty.py             # BEX/JNL regime analysis
```

**24 files total** across 7 modules.

---

## Module Summary

### 1. Data Acquisition — [download.py](file:///c:/Users/Dell/OneDrive/Desktop/BTP/data/download.py)

| Source | Function | Fallback |
|--------|----------|----------|
| S&P 500 tickers | Wikipedia scrape | — |
| Stock prices (monthly OHLCV) | `yfinance` | — |
| Risk-free rate (3M T-Bill) | FRED `TB3MS` | 2% proxy |
| Chen & Zimmermann chars | OpenAssetPricing.com | Synthetic |
| Welch & Goyal 14 macro factors | Google Sheets export | Synthetic |
| BEX/JNL uncertainty | FRED VIX proxy | Synthetic |

---

### 2. Feature Engineering

#### [firm_chars.py](file:///c:/Users/Dell/OneDrive/Desktop/BTP/features/firm_chars.py)
Filters C&Z dataset to **124 characteristics** with ≥40% non-missing values, ranked by coverage.

#### [macro.py](file:///c:/Users/Dell/OneDrive/Desktop/BTP/features/macro.py)
- PCA on 14 macro factors → **3 principal components** (99.9% variance explained)
- **496 interaction terms**: 124 chars × (3 PCs + 1 constant)
- Final: 496 interactions + 14 raw macro = **510 covariates**

#### [technical.py](file:///c:/Users/Dell/OneDrive/Desktop/BTP/features/technical.py)
All **39 technical indicators** implemented from scratch (no TA-Lib dependency):

| # | Indicators | Count |
|---|-----------|-------|
| 1 | Bollinger Bands (MA, Upper, Lower, Width, %) | 5 |
| 2 | DMI+, DMI−, ADX, ADXR | 4 |
| 3 | EMA, CCI, Fear/Greed, Hurst | 4 |
| 4 | Min, Max, Retracement | 3 |
| 5 | Momentum, Momentum MA | 2 |
| 6 | MACD, Signal, Diff | 3 |
| 7 | MA Envelopes | 1 |
| 8 | MA Oscillator, Signal, Diff | 3 |
| 9 | ROC, Parabolic SAR, RSI, SMA | 4 |
| 10 | Stochastics %K, %D, %DS, %DSS | 4 |
| 11 | Trender Up/Down | 2 |
| 12 | Triangular MA, Variable MA, Weighted MA, Williams %R | 4 |
| **Total** | | **39** |

---

### 3. Preprocessing — [pipeline.py](file:///c:/Users/Dell/OneDrive/Desktop/BTP/preprocessing/pipeline.py)

1. **Feature exclusion**: Drop columns with >60% missing
2. **Forward fill**: Per-stock temporal fill
3. **Cross-sectional mean imputation**: Monthly mean across all firms

---

### 4. Models

| Model | File | Key Hyperparameters |
|-------|------|-------------------|
| OLS | [linear.py](file:///c:/Users/Dell/OneDrive/Desktop/BTP/models/linear.py) | Kitchen-sink 510 predictors |
| LASSO | [linear.py](file:///c:/Users/Dell/OneDrive/Desktop/BTP/models/linear.py) | λ = 1e-3 |
| Decision Tree | [tree.py](file:///c:/Users/Dell/OneDrive/Desktop/BTP/models/tree.py) | CART with greedy splits |
| Random Forest | [tree.py](file:///c:/Users/Dell/OneDrive/Desktop/BTP/models/tree.py) | 50 trees, depth 8 |
| GBRT/XGBoost | [boosting.py](file:///c:/Users/Dell/OneDrive/Desktop/BTP/models/boosting.py) | 50 trees, LR grid-tuned |
| Deep-NN | [deep_nn.py](file:///c:/Users/Dell/OneDrive/Desktop/BTP/models/deep_nn.py) | 64→32→16→8→4, ReLU, Adam |

---

### 5. Training — [rolling_window.py](file:///c:/Users/Dell/OneDrive/Desktop/BTP/training/rolling_window.py)

Expanding window with 12-month shifts:
- **Iteration 1**: Train 1990–2005, Test 2006
- **Iteration 2**: Train 1990–2006, Test 2007
- **...**
- **Iteration 16**: Train 1990–2020, Test 2021

Metrics per iteration: **R²_OOS**, **MSE**, **MAE**

---

### 6. Analysis

| Analysis | File | What it does |
|----------|------|-------------|
| SHAP | [shap_analysis.py](file:///c:/Users/Dell/OneDrive/Desktop/BTP/analysis/shap_analysis.py) | DeepExplainer on Deep-NN → mean &vert;SHAP&vert; for 39 TIs |
| Portfolio Sorts | [portfolio_sorts.py](file:///c:/Users/Dell/OneDrive/Desktop/BTP/analysis/portfolio_sorts.py) | Quintile sorts → H-L R²_OOS per TI |
| DM Test | [dm_test.py](file:///c:/Users/Dell/OneDrive/Desktop/BTP/analysis/dm_test.py) | Full (510) vs TI-only (39) forecast comparison |
| Uncertainty | [uncertainty.py](file:///c:/Users/Dell/OneDrive/Desktop/BTP/analysis/uncertainty.py) | R²_OOS in high/low BEX & JNL regimes |

---

## How to Run

```bash
# 1. Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# 2. Run entire pipeline
python main.py --all

# 3. Or run individual steps
python main.py --download     # Download data only
python main.py --features     # Build features only
python main.py --train        # Train models only
python main.py --analyze      # Run analysis only
```

Results are saved to [results/](file:///c:/Users/Dell/OneDrive/Desktop/BTP/training/rolling_window.py#185-220) including CSV tables and PNG plots.

> [!NOTE]
> The pipeline includes synthetic data fallbacks for all external sources. If any download fails (C&Z, W&G, FRED), the pipeline will automatically generate synthetic data and continue running, clearly logging which sources used real vs. synthetic data.
